{
  "_meta": {
    "table": "asset_manifest",
    "source": "docs/VISUAL_STYLE.md, section 4",
    "notes": [
      "One entry per logical asset. Code asks the Assets autoload for an id and never names a file.",
      "file is a path under the project (for example assets/models/creatures/giant_bat.glb). Leave it empty for assets that are built in code by design. If a file is named but missing or broken, the stand-in is used and one warning is logged.",
      "placeholder.builder names a procedural stand-in in scripts/visual/stand_ins.gd. A stand-in is a real model built in code, not a bare primitive.",
      "target_height is in metres; a loaded file is scaled to it and its base dropped to y = 0. It is not applied to stand-ins, which are built to size.",
      "toonify, outline_px, cast_shadow and palette_remap are read from Pass 1 (toon material and outlines).",
      "source, url, license and attribution feed CREDITS.md (python3 tools/build_credits.py). Every third-party file needs all four; prefer CC0, then CC-BY with credit.",
      "clips maps the game's animation names to the names inside the file. Fill it from tools/inspect_model.gd output, never by guessing."
    ]
  },
